    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Teads is navigating a mixed demand environment, with overall ad revenue contracting but connected TV (CTV) revenue growing robustly, signaling a strategic shift toward higher-value inventory. Ex-TAC gross profit improved and the pace of decline in key metrics slowed, pointing to better revenue quality, though top-line stabilization remains elusive. Competitive pressure from larger ad-tech players and advertiser caution amid a choppy macro backdrop weigh on sentiment. The company’s “attention science” narrative offers differentiation, but the market remains skeptical whether CTV momentum can fully offset persistent weakness in legacy display and broader digital ad spending.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership reaffirmed its full-year profitability target, projecting confidence that a back-half recovery will materialize despite a very weak first quarter. The quarter’s cash outflow was exacerbated by a semiannual bond interest payment and seasonal working capital, underscoring the strain from a high debt load. By issuing quarterly ex-TAC guidance, management aims to provide transparency and anchor expectations, though credibility is fragile given the wide gap between near-term performance and ambitious annual goals. The recent stock rally reflects tentative optimism, but execution on CTV growth and disciplined cost management will be critical to restoring durable confidence.",
